**Read:** [Groundwater — Freeze and Cherry, preserved authorized edition](../sources/Groundwater-Freeze-Cherry.lingua#r_6P2FK74P9MC2672X94GE1S0NZB), the complete chemical-properties, geochemical-evolution, transport, and relevant karst/geological sections; [Physical Geology, second edition — Steven Earle](../sources/Physical-Geology-Earle.lingua#r_5GWEYVQGR176TXMQT0S881ZSKX), chapter 14’s chemistry, karst, and contamination context; [Use carbonate chemistry to connect gas, acid/base, and mineral equilibria](../../../../hephaestus/chemistry/general-chemistry/aqueous/Carbonate-water-and-open-boundaries.lingua#r_0WTZ0V8V2K18X7XJZQFAQ4KB07), the full shared carbonate/open-boundary explanation.

Water composition reflects inputs, mineral/gas interactions, redox conditions, mixing, exchange, residence distributions, and reactions along pathways. A concentration is evidence at a place/time under a sampling method, not a unique label for the entire aquifer's origin or age.

Return to [Use carbonate chemistry to connect gas, acid/base, and mineral equilibria](../../../../hephaestus/chemistry/general-chemistry/aqueous/Carbonate-water-and-open-boundaries.lingua#r_0WTZ0V8V2K18X7XJZQFAQ4KB07) for carbonate speciation and open/closed CO₂ boundaries. Dissolution can enlarge pathways in soluble rocks, producing karst with strongly heterogeneous conduits and storage. A uniform porous-medium approximation may miss the travel times and connections most important to a question.

Distinguish advection, dispersion/diffusion, sorption, reaction, and production/decay. A conservative tracer and a reactive dissolved species can move differently in the same flow field. A reported groundwater age can be an apparent model age or a mixture of waters with different histories, requiring interpretation rather than a direct travel-time label.

**Work:** build a conceptual flow-and-reaction account for a documented aquifer example using its stratigraphy, structures, head observations, and chemistry. Check charge balance and units where the supplied data permit, preserving detection limits and method uncertainty. Compare mixing with reaction as explanations for a composition trend; identify a discriminating measurement rather than inferring a unique process from correlation.

Read the full relevant geochemistry/transport chapters and the basic groundwater treatment first. Later hydrogeology/geochemistry studies deepen inverse models and tracer interpretation. Engineering water supply, mine drainage, and environmental questions will reuse this material with their own site-specific evidence and purpose.

**Continue:** [Explain slope movement through geometry, materials, water, and time](../surface/Slopes-mass-movement-and-ground-change.lingua#r_0EQ7KNWABCS4RHYP8WAA4YM0K0).

